{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Recurred during fe94's pre-push `make verify` on this host. Evidence confirming the diagnosis rather than restating it:\n\n- Default tier: 20,405 passed, 27 skipped, 0 failed. Integration tier: 1 failed, 202 passed, 3 skipped — this test, alone.\n- `which git-remote-s3` → `/Users/joeoakhart/.local/bin/git-remote-s3` (a separate install, outside the worktree venv). `.venv/bin/python -c \"import git_remote_s3\"` → `ModuleNotFoundError`. So the guard's condition is true while the body's condition is false, which is the whole bug.\n- The test body at `tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py:683-688` touches only the Python module — `git_remote_s3`, `S3Remote`, `parse_git_url`, `Doctor`. It never invokes the binary. The guard at `:679-682` is therefore not a proxy that happens to diverge; it tests a condition the test does not depend on at all.\n- `git diff origin/main -- tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py` is empty, so this reproduces on unmodified `main` for any host in this state. It is not caused by the change under verification.\n- It is the only `skipif` in the file (`grep -n \"skipif\" ` returns one hit), so there is no sibling using a correct guard to copy.\n\nThe fix is to guard on what the body uses: `pytest.importorskip(\"git_remote_s3\")` in the body, or `importlib.util.find_spec(\"git_remote_s3\") is None` in the `skipif`. The binary check can go — nothing in the test runs it.\n\nNot fixed here: fe94's commit is a plan-review criterion touching 4 unrelated files, and widening its `file_impact` to carry this fix would invalidate its current plan-review certificate and force a re-review."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793680257352100240,"uuid":"d762102a-80f5-4231-af17-45911529d652"}